# SDK Hooks

Files in `cldprovisioning/internal/hooks/` are NOT regenerated by Speakeasy (except `hooks.go`) — custom files are safe to edit.

## Custom files

- `registration.go` — hook registration, only generated once
- `cloudinary_hook.go` — CloudinaryAccountHook (SDKInit + BeforeRequest)
- `account_config.go` — env var parsing (CLOUDINARY_ACCOUNT_URL + individual vars)
- `user_agent_hook.go` — custom user-agent header

## User-Agent Format

Pattern: `Cloudinary/AccountProvisioning Go/{sdkVersion} Gen/{genVersion} Schema/{schemaVersion} (Go {goVersion}; {os} {arch})`

## AccountConfig (CLOUDINARY_ACCOUNT_URL)

`account_config.go` parses `CLOUDINARY_ACCOUNT_URL` with format: `account://<api_key>:<api_secret>@<account_id>`

Individual env vars (`CLOUDINARY_ACCOUNT_ID`, `CLOUDINARY_PROVISIONING_API_KEY`, `CLOUDINARY_PROVISIONING_API_SECRET`) override URL-parsed values.

## Hook lifecycle

1. `SDKInit` — fills `AccountID` from env/URL if not explicitly provided; replaces User-Agent string
2. `BeforeRequest` — resolves credentials from explicit security params or env config, sets Basic Auth header
